Fan-out latency values printed by remote consumers are not evidence because producer timestamps originate on TX and consumer timestamps originate on RX while clock_sync.method=none. This phase measures delivery and scaling only.

The first 500k three-receiver attempt was rejected before traffic because sequential readiness checks exceeded 30-second process idle windows. Commit e5fb156 added a manifest-recorded 120-second startup allowance and source revision. The subsequent failures listed above occur after traffic starts and are capacity failures, not startup failures.
